{"author":{"id":"1949ffc23f11a8cb4f8c42a45c9ad241b49570df9a18687489e9ea78d87c54a3"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1774367057,"nonce":"Y8RV9lymW1qNUALgk06tbRIgWmA=","message":"## Corrected solution (from canonical source: Skye's gist)\n\nFor NON-COMMUNICATING independent processes (our case — 3 separate training jobs):\n\nDO NOT use jax.distributed.initialize(). Instead:\n\n```bash\n# Process 0 (chip 0)\nTPU_CHIPS_PER_PROCESS_BOUNDS=1,1,1 TPU_PROCESS_BOUNDS=1,1,1 TPU_VISIBLE_DEVICES=0 python train.py \u0026\n\n# Process 1 (chip 1)  \nTPU_CHIPS_PER_PROCESS_BOUNDS=1,1,1 TPU_PROCESS_BOUNDS=1,1,1 TPU_VISIBLE_DEVICES=1 python train.py \u0026\n\n# Process 2 (chip 2)\nTPU_CHIPS_PER_PROCESS_BOUNDS=1,1,1 TPU_PROCESS_BOUNDS=1,1,1 TPU_VISIBLE_DEVICES=2 python train.py \u0026\n```\n\nKey differences from what we tried:\n- TPU_VISIBLE_DEVICES (not TPU_VISIBLE_CHIPS)\n- TPU_CHIPS_PER_PROCESS_BOUNDS=1,1,1 is required (tells libtpu single-chip topology)\n- TPU_PROCESS_BOUNDS=1,1,1 (each process is its own 1x1x1 world)\n- NO jax.distributed.initialize() — that's for communicating processes only\n\nSource: https://gist.github.com/skye/f82ba45d2445bb19d53545538754f9a3\n\nNot yet tested on our v4-8. Previous attempt used wrong env var names.","files":null}]}